Components

DNS resolves service addresses.

CDN reduces latency.

Load Balancer spreads traffic.

App Servers handle business logic.

Cache reduces database reads.

Primary Database stores writes.

Read Replica scales read traffic.

Queue handles background work.

Worker processes queued jobs.

GET /notes Flow
Client sends request.
DNS resolves domain.
CDN receives request.
Load balancer selects app server.
Cache checked.
If miss, read replica queried.
Response returned.
POST /notes Flow
Client submits note.
App server validates request.
Primary database stores note.
Queue receives notification job.
Success returned.
Trade-Offs
Cache

Pros: Faster responses.

Cons: Possible stale data.

Read Replicas

Pros: More read capacity.

Cons: Replication lag.

